<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Djerba</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Jerba</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Djerba is an island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-gabes">Gulf of Gabès</a> off southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>, the largest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. Long a trading and fishing centre, it has an ancient Jewish community and an Ibadi Muslim population. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was repeatedly fought over by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, Aragon and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hafsid-dynasty">Hafsids</a>, and later by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, notably in the Battle of Djerba of 1560.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/djerba.jpg" alt="Djerba" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA Earth Observatory images by Lauren Dauphin, using Landsat data from the U.S. Geological Survey. Story by Adam Voiland. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Djerba_Island.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
